      "worked_solution": "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QRP+m∠HRQ & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {155}^{∘}+m∠HRQ & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HRQ & ={25}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△QHR$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠RQH+m∠HRQ+m∠QHR & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠RQH+{25}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠RQH+{115}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠RQH & ={65}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
